dified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-07-17T07:42:55.983744"}}},"ISBN:9781472590817":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781472590817","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL48658456M/Sacred_Objects_in_Secular_Spaces","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL48658456M/Sacred_Objects_in_Secular_Spaces","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL8075368A","name":"Bruce M. Sullivan"}],"isbn_13":["9781472590817"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["BL603"],"pagination":"256","publish_date":"2015","publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc"],"source_records":["bwb:9781472590817"],"subjects":["Religious articles","Art, exhibitions"],"title":"Sacred Objects in Secular Spaces","weight":"0.468","subtitle":"Exhibiting Asian Religions in Museums","full_title":"Sacred Objects in Secular Spaces Exhibiting Asian Religions in Museums","works":[{"key":"/works/OL21101142W"}],"key":"/books/OL48658456M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-07-17T07:19:49.777335"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-07-17T07:19:49.777335"}}},"ISBN:9781472590800":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781472590800","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28563044M/Sacred_Objects_in_Secular_Spaces","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28563044M/Sacred_Objects_in_Secular_Spaces","details":{"publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc"],"subtitle":"Exhibiting Asian Religions in Museums","source_records":["bwb:9781472590800","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part42.utf8:63324623:5536","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-024.mrc:46171497:3850","marc:marc_bloomsbury/2025MAR_bloomsbury.mrc:47083813:6063","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2025-03-17:T5-DGH-866","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_042.bib.mrc:132559976:7522"],"title":"Sacred Objects in Secular Spaces","lccn":["2015019640"],"number_of_pages":216,"isbn_13":["9781472590800"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["BL603","AM7 .S23 2015"],"publish_date":"2015","key":"/books/OL28563044M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL8075368A","name":"Bruce M. Sullivan"},{"key":"/authors/OL7739581A","name":"Bruce Sullivan"}],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL21101142W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["Religious articles","Art, exhibitions"],"oclc_numbers":["897016326","921302086"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"We have long recognized that many objects in museums were originally on display in temples, shrines, or monasteries, and were religiously significant to the communities that created and used them. How, though, are such objects to be understood, described, exhibited, and handled now that they are in museums? Are they still sacred objects, or formerly sacred objects that are now art objects, or are they simultaneously objects of religious and artistic significance, depending on who is viewing the object? These objects not only raise questions about their own identities, but also about the ways we understand the religious traditions in which these objects were created and which they represent in museums today. Bringing together religious studies scholars and museum curators, Sacred Objects in Secular Spaces is the first v. to focus on Asian religions in relation to these questions. The contributors analyze an array of issues related to the exhibition in museums of objects of religious significance from Hindu, Buddhist, and Sikh traditions. The 'lives' of objects are considered, along with the categories of 'sacred' and 'profane,' 'religious' and 'secular.' As interest in material manifestations of religious ideas and practices continues to grow, Sacred Objects in Secular Spaces is a much-needed contribution to religious and Asian studies, anthropology of religion and museums studies.\"--Bloomsbury Publishing."},"identifiers":{"doi":["10.5040/9781474256346"]},"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:T5-DGH-866"],"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-04T14:48:43.773183"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-07-09T12:29:01.828242"}}},"ISBN:9781472529978":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781472529978","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL37166873M/Sikhs_Across_Borders","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL37166873M/Sikhs_Across_Borders","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7912034A","name":"Knut A. Jacobsen"},{"key":"/authors/OL6838946A","name":"Kristina Myrvold"}],"isbn_13":["9781472529978"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["BL2018.S4745 2014"],"pagination":"240","publish_date":"2014","publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc"],"source_records":["bwb:9781472529978"],"subjects":["Sikhism","Emigration and immigration","Sikhs","Europe, emigration and immigration"],"title":"Sikhs Across Borders","weight":"0.409","subtitle":"Transnational Practices of European Sikhs","full_title":"Sikhs Across Borders Transnational Practices of European Sikhs","works":[{"key":"/works/OL16636821W"}],"key":"/books/OL37166873M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-02-26T15:26:28.577181"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-02-26T15:26:28.577181"}}},"ISBN:9781441170873":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781441170873","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL25316263M/Sikhs_across_borders","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL25316263M/Sikhs_across_borders","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13884051-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Continuum International Publishing Group","Bloomsbury Academic"],"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Migration, settlement and challenges in the diaspora","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Constructing identities, representations and belongings","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Learning, teaching and contesting religious beliefs and practices.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"lc_classifications":["BL2018 .S4745 2012","BL2018.S4745 2012"],"key":"/books/OL25316263M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL538467A","name":"Knut A. Jacobsen"},{"key":"/authors/OL6838946A","name":"Kristina Myrvold"}],"subtitle":"transnational practices of European Sikhs","publish_places":["New York"],"edition_name":"First [edition].","pagination":"pages cm","source_records":["marc:marc_loc_updates/v40.i20.records.utf8:13370759:1325","marc:marc_loc_updates/v40.i21.records.utf8:12275061:1325","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part39.utf8:184385960:1323","bwb:9781441113870","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:415144206:1484","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-020.mrc:56903576:1524","amazon:1441113878","bwb:9781441170873","marc:marc_bloomsbury/2025MAR_bloomsbury.mrc:48166666:3446","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_046.bib.mrc:272859007:2455"],"title":"Sikhs across borders","lccn":["2012011037"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},"isbn_13":["9781441113870","9781441170873"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"dewey_decimal_class":["294.6094"],"subject_places":["Europe"],"subjects":["Emigration and immigration","Sikhism","Sikhs"],"publish_date":"2012","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"edited by Knut A. Jacobsen and Kristina Myrvold","works":[{"key":"/works/OL16636821W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["777652865","1166565522"],"covers":[13884051],"number_of_pages":240,"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Sikhs Across Borders is the first study to explore patterns of transnational practices among European Sikhs, with particular focus on the links between the Sikhs in Europe, Punjab (the 'home-land') and within a global Sikh community. The book illustrates how local and transnational spheres coexist and interact in a multitude of social and cultural practices and discourses among European Sikhs past and present. Based on new empirical research Sikhs Across Borders book explores how religion continues to play a significant role in the daily lives of European Sikhs and is important for their maintenance of links with the homeland, as well as Sikhs in other parts of the world. The team of international contributors show how Sikhs are shaping new self-representations and identity constructions through a multitude of transnational practices on the individual, national and global level, such as marriages, pilgrimage narratives, and the use of the internet and new media. Further transnational practices examined include religious learning and teaching practices and responses to political events in the diaspora.\"--Bloomsbury Publishing."},"identifiers":{"doi":["10.5040/9781472548689"]},"latest_revision":10,"revision":10,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2012-05-16T09:27:39.086467"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-09-07T10:55:24.628606"}}},"ISBN:9781441113870":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781441113870","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL25316263M/Sikhs_across_borders","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL25316263M/Sikhs_across_borders","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13884051-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Continuum International Publishing Group","Bloomsbury Academic"],"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Migration, settlement and challenges in the diaspora","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Constructing identities, representations and belongings","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Learning, teaching and contesting religious beliefs and practices.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"lc_classifications":["BL2018 .S4745 2012","BL2018.S4745 2012"],"key":"/books/OL25316263M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/